Subject: [PATCH] HID: multitouch: add device ID for the T1 Apple Touch Bar

The Touch Bar digitizer on T1 MacBook Pros (MacBookPro13,x and 14,x, the
2016 and 2017 models) is the same device class as the T2's, exposed on the
iBridge's 05ac:8600 rather than 05ac:8302.

Its report descriptor, read from a MacBookPro13,2 in USB configuration 2, is
a Digitizers/TouchPad application collection containing ten Finger
collections of

    TransducerIndex : 4 bits
    Touch           : 1 bit
    InRange         : 1 bit
    (padding)       : 2 bits
    X               : 16 bits, logical max 32767
    Y               : 8 bits,  logical max 127

followed by a vendor 0xff11 collection with a 64-bit timestamp and a 32-bit
report counter, for a 52-byte input report with no report ID and no
HID_DG_CONTACTMAX field.

That is exactly what MT_CLS_APPLE_TOUCHBAR already describes, so only the
device ID is needed. Verified on a MacBookPro13,2 running 7.1.9: with this
entry the digitizer binds to hid-multitouch, gains INPUT_PROP_DIRECT and the
ABS_MT_* axes, and tiny-dfr drives the Touch Bar.

NOTE FOR REBASING: this is written against the tree that carries
MT_CLS_APPLE_TOUCHBAR (Linux 6.15 and later). Regenerate with git format-patch
against a real tree before sending upstream; the context below is
reconstructed, not taken from a checkout.

If USB_DEVICE_ID_APPLE_IBRIDGE is not yet present in drivers/hid/hid-ids.h,
the first hunk adds it.

---
 drivers/hid/hid-ids.h       | 1 +
 drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/hid/hid-ids.h
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-ids.h
@@
 #define USB_DEVICE_ID_APPLE_TOUCHBAR_BACKLIGHT 0x8102
 #define USB_DEVICE_ID_APPLE_TOUCHBAR_DISPLAY 0x8302
+#define USB_DEVICE_ID_APPLE_IBRIDGE	0x8600

--- a/drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c
@@ static const struct hid_device_id mt_devices[] = {
 	{ .driver_data = MT_CLS_APPLE_TOUCHBAR,
 		HID_USB_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_APPLE,
 			       USB_DEVICE_ID_APPLE_TOUCHBAR_DISPLAY) },
+
+	/* Apple Touch Bar on T1 Macs (MacBookPro13,x and 14,x) */
+	{ .driver_data = MT_CLS_APPLE_TOUCHBAR,
+		HID_USB_DEVICE(USB_VENDOR_ID_APPLE,
+			       USB_DEVICE_ID_APPLE_IBRIDGE) },
